44|   dbs: {},\r\n        ^^^^^^^^^^\r\n...\r\n  2597|   }\r\n        ^^^\r\n  2598| };\r\n        ^\r\n\r\n1 error(s), 0 warning(s)\r\n\r\nem++: error: closure compiler failed (rc: 1): /home/runner/work/_temp/a4c0fc0c-267b-47e7-87b3-d936492b9bdd/emsdk-main/node/22.16.0_64bit/bin/node --max_old_space_size=8192 /home/runner/work/_temp/a4c0fc0c-267b-47e7-87b3-d936492b9bdd/emsdk-main/upstream/emscripten/node_modules/.bin/google-closure-compiler --compilation_level ADVANCED_OPTIMIZATIONS --language_in UNSTABLE --language_out NO_TRANSPILE --emit_use_strict=false --assume_static_inheritance_is_not_used=false --externs /home/runner/work/_temp/a4c0fc0c-267b-47e7-87b3-d936492b9bdd/emsdk-main/upstream/emscripten/src/closure-externs/closure-externs.js --externs /home/runner/work/_temp/a4c0fc0c-267b-47e7-87b3-d936492b9bdd/emsdk-main/upstream/emscripten/src/closure-externs/modularize-externs.js --externs /home/runner/work/godot/godot/modules/webxr/native/webxr.externs.js --externs /home/runner/work/godot/godot/platform/web/js/libs/library_godot_webgl2.externs.js --js /tmp/emscripten_temp_vv1u9jsp/godot.web.template_release.wasm32.jso2.js --js_output_file tmpoq9u13dw.cc.js the error message may be clearer with -g1 and EMCC_DEBUG=2 set\r\n```\r\n\r\n~We should really add this option to at least one CI build.~\r\n*Edit:* Well nevermind, we did, that's why CI is failing :P","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2970895256/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":1,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2971864688","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107460#issuecomment-2971864688","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107460","id":2971864688,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6xIw5w","user":{"login":"adamscott","id":270928,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3MDkyOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270928?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott","html_url":"https://github.com/adamscott","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-13T22:25:03Z","updated_at":"2025-06-13T22:25:13Z","body":"@akien-mga After a deep investigation, I found out the issue. It stems from Emscripten. [I created an Emscripten PR to fix the issue.](https://github.com/emscripten-core/emscripten/pull/24567)","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2971864688/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2974664091","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107460#issuecomment-2974664091","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107460","id":2974664091,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6xTcWb","user":{"login":"adamscott","id":270928,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3MDkyOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270928?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott","html_url":"https://github.com/adamscott","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-15T19:54:04Z","updated_at":"2025-06-15T19:54:04Z","body":"@akien-mga emscripten-core/emscripten#24567 has been merged, so when 4.0.11 will come out, I'll update this PR to make it the CI target.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2974664091/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":2,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2987975178","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107460#issuecomment-2987975178","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107460","id":2987975178,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6yGOIK","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-19T12:42:44Z","updated_at":"2025-06-19T12:42:44Z","body":"I just tested WebXR in Godot 4.5-beta1 (which I try to do for all releases) and it's currently broken there.\r\n\r\nI think because https://github.com/godotengine/build-containers/pull/151 was merged, updating the version of Emscripten used to make the official builds, but this PR making WebXR compatible with newer Emscripten still hasn't been merged. At least from the error I'm getting in the console, it seems like the issue that the WebXR changes here fix\r\n\r\nHowever, if Emscripten 4.0.10 breaks compiling with Closure, and we use Closure in the official builds, I'm not sure how that could be? So, perhaps I'm incorrect about the cause","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2987975178/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2988470102","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107460#issuecomment-2988470102","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107460","id":2988470102,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6yIG9W","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-19T15:19:16Z","updated_at":"2025-06-19T15:19:16Z","body":"4.5 beta 1 was built with Emscripten 4.0.10 indeed, and with the closure compiler for the `target=editor` build.\r\nThere was no build issue there.\r\n\r\nSo can it be that the closure compiler bug we ran into with recent Emscripten is specifically triggered by changes in this PR?\r\n\r\nAnd indeed it was my bad for merging https://github.com/godotengine/build-containers/pull/151 before this PR, I needed it as a pre-requisite for visionOS builds, and thought this PR would be merged sooner. But we're stuck on the closure compiler issue.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2988470102/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2991180590","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107460#issuecomment-2991180590","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107460","id":2991180590,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6yScsu","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-20T11:45:53Z","updated_at":"2025-06-20T11:45:53Z","body":"So official builds didn't have an issue because we only set `use_closure_compiler=yes` for `target=editor` - which is one we don't here on CI.\r\nOn the other hand on CI we're using `use_closure_compiler=yes` for templates build, which doesn't match how we build official templates, but was added to help catch errors that would appear on the official editor build.\r\n\r\nI don't really know what are the advantages/tradeoffs of the closure compiler, and whether we should start using it for official templates too, or if it's more hassle than worth given potential Emscripten issues as we see here.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2991180590/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2991306571","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107460#issuecomment-2991306571","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107460","id":2991306571,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6yS7dL","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-20T12:11:38Z","updated_at":"2025-06-20T12:11:38Z","body":"> So official builds didn't have an issue because we only set `use_closure_compiler=yes` for `target=editor`\r\n\r\nOh, interesting! I had thought we used it for release template builds. Did we used to do that? I vaguely recall fixing WebXR issues that only came up with Closure back in the Godot 3.x era, but maybe that was folks custom compiling the templates.\r\n\r\n> I don't really know what are the advantages/tradeoffs of the closure compiler, and whether we should start using it for official templates too, or if it's more hassle than worth given potential Emscripten issues as we see here.\r\n\r\nWhen it works, it _should_ generate smaller and faster code, although, we should actually measure that.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2991306571/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2994101748","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107460#issuecomment-2994101748","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107460","id":2994101748,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ydl30","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-22T10:14:43Z","updated_at":"2025-06-22T10:14:43Z","body":"So what should we do here? Waiting for Emscripten 4.0.11 to be released to fix our WebXR support doesn't sound great. And that would also imply that we'd need to make 4.0.11 our minimum supported version, unless we use a different min version depending on whether the closure compiler is used.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2994101748/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2994163701","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107460#issuecomment-2994163701","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107460","id":2994163701,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6yd0_1","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-22T12:26:04Z","updated_at":"2025-06-22T12:26:04Z","body":"Is changing the official builds back to using an Emscripten 3.x version an option? It sounds like there's lots of issues with different 4.x versions. Do we depend on anything from 4.0.0+?\r\n\r\nIf we pick a 3.x later than 3.1.71, it should work with the WebXR changes in this PR.\r\n\r\nAnd, if we're compatible with 4.0.11, folks should be able to start using that in custom builds once it comes out.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2994163701/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3045665051","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107460#issuecomment-3045665051","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107460","id":3045665051,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc61iSkb","user":{"login":"adamscott","id":270928,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3MDkyOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270928?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott","html_url":"https://github.com/adamscott","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-07T15:41:20Z","updated_at":"2025-07-07T15:41:20Z","body":"> Is changing the official builds back to using an Emscripten 3.x version an option? It sounds like there's lots of issues with different 4.x versions. Do we depend on anything from 4.0.0+?\r\n\r\nYes. We depend on 4.0.9 to fix https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104497 which is a release blocker. That's why I think we should just mark 4.0.11 as our minimum target. (I'm waiting anxiously for it to release ASAP)","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3045665051/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3048765845","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107460#issuecomment-3048765845","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107460","id":3048765845,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc61uHmV","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-08T12:32:21Z","updated_at":"2025-07-08T12:32:21Z","body":"> > Do we depend on anything from 4.0.0+?\r\n> \r\n> Yes. We depend on 4.0.9 to fix #104497 which is a release blocker.\r\n\r\n@akien-mga wrote [above](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107460#issuecomment-2968321719):\r\n\r\n> We could keep support for < 4.0.9 by checking it and disabling `lto=thin` if that's what's configured, printing a warning and upgrading it to `lto=full`, which should solve the bug.\r\n\r\nSo, there is a path to supporting versions earlier than 4.0.9 if we want to.\r\n\r\nMy worry with regard to waiting for 4.0.11 is that it may not come before we want to release, or come at the very last minute meaning WebXR doesn't get much testing during beta or rc (and we miss some issue), or that 4.0.11 has some other new issue (which we may or may not notice right away due to how late it would be coming in).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3048765845/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3074494051","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107460#issuecomment-3074494051","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107460","id":3074494051,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc63QQ5j","user":{"login":"michaelharmonart","id":15620900,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1NjIwOTAw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15620900?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelharmonart","html_url":"https://github.com/michaelharmonart","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelharmonart/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelharmonart/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelharmonart/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelharmonart/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelharmonart/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelharmonart/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelharmonart/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelharmonart/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelharmonart/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-15T17:16:16Z","updated_at":"2025-07-15T17:16:16Z","body":"https://github.com/emscripten-core/emsdk/releases/tag/4.0.11\r\n\r\n4.0.11 Has been released","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/